o make the ua  even safer but if the ua really is  so safe if it's like the safest place  for the students and their  families then does it make sense for  deku to leave  on the one hand he is protecting his  friends from a potential villain attack  but on the other hand if deku takes  himself  out of a safe area like the ua he could  be playing right into the hands of the  villains  deku may be making his friends safer by  leaving but he is also putting the  entire world in danger  by making it a lot easier for all for  one to potentially steal  one for all keeping one for all away  from all for one is  obviously in the best interest of  everyone  so by leaving a safe zone like the ua  deku is taking a huge risk  if all for one can get to him and steal  one for all  then it's pretty much game over the hero  society as it is right now  could not possibly stop a villain who  controls both one for all  and all for one and besides even though  deku is definitely the biggest target at  ua because of one for all he is still  not the  only target for the villains there are  plenty of other students and teachers at  ua who are well known to the villains  and whom the villains would love to take  out either for revenge or to prevent  them from posing a threat  in the future this includes bakugou  todoroki the big three  aizawa and many many more like yeah the  villains really want  deku but it's not like they would  completely lose interest in potentially  attacking the ua  just because deku left oh and that  reminds me how does the ua trader plot  point come into play here  has horikoshi completely abandoned this  plot point from the past  or is it about to finally become  relevant again  with the ua now being transformed into  what is essentially a maximum security  bunker  having a spy inside the ua is more  useful now to the villains than  ever before so are they about to  activate the trader once again  and if they do what will that mean for  the story  man i have been wondering about the ua  trader for almost  4 years now and i really hope that this  plot point will have some sort of payoff  eventually  by the way let me know down in the  comments whether you think that there is  a ua trader in the first place  and if you think that there is then who  do you think it is  i know that toru hagakure is a popular  option because her quirk allows her to  be the perfect spy  but my own personal theory is that it  could be principal  nezu i don't think that he is doing it  willingly i think that back when he was  experimented on by humans  ujjiko was somehow involved in those  experiments  and i think that he could have done  something to nezu that allows the  villains to get information from him  without nezu even realizing it  but that's all speculation without more  clues so let me know what you guys think  what are your theories  i'm always interested in hearing more  about the ua trader  now back to deku deku becoming a  vigilante  allows him to be more flexible and  independent in his actions  but he is still going to keep fighting  the villains and we saw him do exactly  that when he used  danger sense to detect muscular and then  stepped in to save shindo  from muscular so yeah it's not like deku  is about to like start hiding so that  all for one can't locate one for all  it's just not how deck  works this means that deku's decision to  become a lone wolf vigilante will expose  him to a lot more danger than if he had  just stayed at ua  but on the other hand this will also  allow deku to set a trap  for all for one if deku had remained  under constant protection  inside the ua he wouldn't have been able  to do much  against the villains but if he starts to  make a reputation for himself as a lone  wolf vigilante who has no official  affiliation to the ua  or the pro heroes system deku will  become the focus of  all of all for one's attention instead  of worrying about the ua and the pro  heroes  all for one will concentrate on tracking  down the lone wolf vigilante deku  by any means necessary but here's the  thing  if deku secretly stays in contact with  his friends at the ua  and with the pro heroes he can  eventually serve as  bait for trapping all for one and the  other villains  if deku can make all for one think that  he is now working completely on his own  all for one will be more likely to come  out of hiding before he and the other  villains are at their strongest  and before shigaraki's procedure has  been perfected i feel like all for one  won't be able to pass up on the  opportunity to steal one for all  from just one lonely kid so all for one  and the other villains are far  more likely to underestimate deku now  that he is on his  own and this could cost them dearly in  the end  so what if this whole decision to leave  the ua  is part of a larger plan right now  time is really working against the  heroes because society is crumbling and  they're spending all of their time  trying to put society back together  meanwhile all for one is probably hiding  somewhere  safe and working on perfecting  shigaraki's transformation  as soon as possible and if shigaraki's  procedure  is perfected it is likely that no one  will be able to stop him  so what if deku just wants to make all  for one think that he is acting as a  lone wolf so that he can lure him  and the other villains out of hiding  before shigaraki becomes virtually  unstoppable if all for one thinks that  he just has to take out one high school  kid and then he can have one for all  he might get reckless and if  all for one comes out of hiding and  attacks deku he could end up walking  right into a trap  laid by the pro heroes and the hero  students in collaboration with  deku so deku might be pretending to be a  lone wolf  but in reality he's working closely with  the other heroes and hero students  in order to bait all for one into a trap  so far we've been led to believe that  deku's decision to leave the ua was  motivated solely by the fact that he  wants to protect his fellow students  from being targeted by the villains  but i think that there might be more to  this decision than meets the eye  i think that deku might be setting an  elaborate trap for all for one and  shigaraki and deku's departure from the  ua  and his decision to become a vigilante  could all be just one part of his secret  master plan  after all if there really is a traitor  inside the ua  and deku is busy concocting a master  plan to take  out the villains it would make sense for  dekku to leave the ua so that his plan  doesn't  leak to the traitor and since deku  doesn't know who the traitor is  he has to assume that almost anyone  could be suspicious  but let me know what you guys think was  deku's decision to leave the ua  and become a lone wolf vigilante just  his way of protecting his friends  or is there more to the story and  if deku really is concocting a secret  master plan  how do you think that this plan will  ultimately unfold  be sure to share your thoughts down in  the comments below  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more boku no hero content  right here on the channel just leave a  like to let me know it only takes a  second but it helps a lot  and if you're new to the channel or  maybe you watch our videos but you just  haven't subscribed yet  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on  all notifications you can also hit me up  on twitter  and instagram at animeopror  a big thank you to all of our anime  uproar patrons for making videos like  this one possible  special thank you to the two disciples  of lord twego himself  alpha sigma and the red-haired raven  and i can't forget all of our the one  tier patrons the ones who rise above  all other clans including ingrata  acquired respect pate heffa liam  thompson algetal  dr cortman dust and scarlet the toasted  chi  bang emperor taku spidey life canal  baked buddhist tungsten tarkis  and